==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|bestial}}, from {{der|en|fro|bestial}}, from {{der|en|LL.|bēstiālis}}, from {{der|en|la|bēstia||beast}} (whence English {{m|en|beast}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɛs.ti.əl/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bestial.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɛs.t͡ʃəl/|/ˈbis.t͡ʃəl/|a=GenAm}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|literally|_|and|_|figuratively}} [[beast|Beast]]-like
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Othello|II|3|text=Reputation, reputation, reputation! O, I have lost my reputation! I have lost the immortal part of myself, and what remains is '''bestial'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|4|lines=753-4|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Paradise_Lost_(1674)/Book_IV|text=By thee adulterous lust was driven from men /<br>Among the '''bestial''' herds to range {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Jekyll and Hyde|text=This familiar that I called out of my own soul, and sent forth alone to do his good pleasure, was a being inherently malign and villainous; his every act and thought centered on self; drinking pleasure with '''bestial''' avidity from any degree of torture to another; relentless like a man of stone.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1900|author=w:Willa Cather|title=Eric Hermannson's Soul|journal=Cosmopolitan|month=April
|passage=His was a '''bestial''' face, a face that bore the stamp of Nature's eternal injustice.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 31 2022|author=Matteo Wong|title=[https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2022/12/avatar-2-movie-navi-constructed-language/672616/ Hollywood’s Love Affair With Fictional Languages]|journal=The Atlantic
|passage=The Game of Thrones novels were best sellers without fleshed-out Dothraki; the languages in Star Wars, one of the most successful franchises ever, are mostly gibberish, even if Han Solo claims to understand Chewbacca’s '''bestial''' warbling.}}

